      "writtenOn": "2019-02-12T14:39:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine, but since it\u0027s protected and used by subclasses, it\u0027s possible that all the callers will be already running on the handler thread. In that case, you\u0027re probably better off removing this post() and just saying (and possibly enforcing with assertions) that callers must be running on the handler thread. If they\u0027re not, they can always post a lambda to the handler thread themselves.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 356,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 356,
        "endChar": 15
      },
